# Parallel Agents (GitHub Flow)

All AI Agents must follow the authoritative multi-agent & GitHub Flow rules in `AGENTS.md`:

- **Isolated worktrees**: Use Git worktree (`/worktree`) or Cloud Agent (`/in-cloud`). Do not share checkouts.
- **Branch naming**: Branch from clean `origin/master` as `feat/<topic>` or `fix/<topic>`. Never push `master`.
- **DDD task splitting**: Split by directory (`internal/domain`, `internal/reporter`, `extensions/cursor`, `docs/`).
- **Single daemon**: Keep only one running `agent-monitor` (`:8000`). Never start duplicate daemons from worktrees.
- **Quality gate & Local AI review**: Run `go test -v -race ./...` and `make review` / `make pre-pr`. Fix any `[BLOCK]` issues before PR creation.
- **Never auto-merge**: Stop immediately after `gh pr create` and presenting the link. Merging requires explicit user authorization (`gh pr merge` is strictly forbidden without user approval).
- Authoritative specification: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) / [docs/PARALLEL_AGENTS.md](docs/PARALLEL_AGENTS.md).
